UPDATE workers SET description='Tomas Andersson is the voice of NET, the lead announcer whose commentary has defined the sound of Poland wrestling for years. With a deep knowledge of the sport and a voice built for broadcasting, Tomas Andersson calls every match with passion and precision, making even the most routine holds feel important. Whether calling a dramatic title change or a quick squash match, Tomas Andersson brings professionalism and energy to every broadcast. Behind the scenes, they''re also a mentor to younger broadcasting talent.' WHERE workerID=9546;
UPDATE workers SET description='Alexander Novak is an official referee for NET, one of the most trusted officials in Poland wrestling. Known for strict rule enforcement and quick three-counts, Alexander Novak has officiated some of the biggest matches in NET history. With a keen eye for interference and a no-nonsense approach to disqualifications, Alexander Novak keeps the matches fair — or at least tries to, when managers and heels don''t get in the way. A good referee is invisible when the match is going well and decisive when it isn''t, and Alexander Novak embodies that philosophy every time they step into the ring.' WHERE workerID=9547;
UPDATE workers SET description='Marco Horvat is a veteran manager in NET, a ringside manipulator whose interference and mind games have cost countless opponents their matches. With decades of experience in Poland wrestling, Marco Horvat knows every trick in the book — the distraction, the foreign object, the timely trip — and uses them all to give their clients the advantage. While not a wrestler themselves, Marco Horvat understands the psychology of the business better than most in-ring performers, and their stable of managed talent is always a threat to any champion.' WHERE workerID=9548;
